WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:15.214
and Bobby walked into Kids Central together.

2
00:00:17.334 --> 00:00:21.336
"My family is going snowboarding again this weekend," Bobby said.

3
00:00:21.356 --> 00:00:23.017
"Want to come?"

4
00:00:23.037 --> 00:00:25.518
"Sure!" Ethan said.

5
00:00:25.538 --> 00:00:28.719
"I'm saving money for my own snowboard."

6
00:00:29.719 --> 00:00:30.900
He opened his backpack.

7
00:00:31.624 --> 00:00:33.805
"Look! This is what I have saved so far."

8
00:00:37.166 --> 00:00:39.866
Bobby looked at the crumpled bills in Ethan's backpack.

9
00:00:40.527 --> 00:00:41.687
"How much do you have?"

10
00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:43.627
Ethan shrugged.

11
00:00:43.647 --> 00:00:46.748
"Mom said I have to save a hundred dollars.

12
00:00:47.128 --> 00:00:48.629
I think I have a long way to go."

13
00:00:48.649 --> 00:00:54.530
"Ethan, you shouldn't bring a lot of money to school," Miss Shelly said.

14
00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:56.171
"You could lose it."

15
00:00:56.191 --> 00:00:59.732
"I don't have anywhere to keep it," Ethan said.

16
00:01:01.032 --> 00:01:03.994
"I keep mine in an old sock," Bobby said.

17
00:01:04.014 --> 00:01:06.655
"Yuck!" Izzie said.

18
00:01:06.675 --> 00:01:08.477
"Smelly money!

19
00:01:08.497 --> 00:01:10.898
I use a piggy bank."

20
00:01:11.939 --> 00:01:13.880
Miss Shelly told everyone to sit down.

21
00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:19.563
"We're going to make wallets today," she said.

22
00:01:19.583 --> 00:01:23.986
"Soon you'll each have a safe, clean place to keep your cash."

23
00:01:25.227 --> 00:01:26.327
"Sounds good to me!"

24
00:01:26.687 --> 00:01:27.348
Ethan said.

25
00:01:28.436 --> 00:01:31.158
Miss Shelly passed out sheets of craft foam and rulers.

26
00:01:31.178 --> 00:01:36.381
"First, fold the sheet five centimeters from the top.

27
00:01:37.722 --> 00:01:39.724
Use the ruler to make a nice crease."

28
00:01:42.065 --> 00:01:43.987
Nina showed Ethan how to make the crease.

29
00:01:44.007 --> 00:01:47.209
"Thanks," Ethan said.

30
00:01:47.229 --> 00:01:49.210
"That makes it easier to fold!"

31
00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:55.234
"Now fold the bottom of the sheet up to that line," Miss Shelly said.

32
00:01:55.254 --> 00:01:57.476
"Crease the fold again.

33
00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:02.243
Then lay the foam flat and punch holes along the bottom."

34
00:02:06.846 --> 00:02:08.287
Bobby grabbed the hole puncher.

35
00:02:08.307 --> 00:02:10.689
"I want to use it first!"

36
00:02:12.691 --> 00:02:14.292
Miss Shelly lifted her eyebrow.

37
00:02:14.312 --> 00:02:17.614
"We'll take turns, Bobby," she said.

38
00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:21.557
"Next fold the wallet up to the line.

39
00:02:22.938 --> 00:02:24.720
Mark matching holes with a pen."

40
00:02:30.348 --> 00:02:31.969
The kids followed her instructions.

41
00:02:31.989 --> 00:02:34.011
"I'm ready to sew!"

42
00:02:34.391 --> 00:02:35.032
Nina said.

43
00:02:35.052 --> 00:02:39.435
"Thread your needle with a double strand of yarn," Miss Shelly said.

44
00:02:39.455 --> 00:02:41.978
"Make a knot in the end.

45
00:02:43.239 --> 00:02:46.401
Then begin sewing the wallet's sides together."

46
00:02:51.926 --> 00:02:54.328
Ethan started sewing at the bottom of one side.

47
00:02:54.348 --> 00:02:56.609
"Wait!" Nina said.

48
00:02:56.629 --> 00:02:59.652
"Start sewing with the yarn on the inside.

49
00:03:00.492 --> 00:03:01.933
Then the knot won't show."

50
00:03:01.953 --> 00:03:05.636
"Oh. Good idea," Ethan said.

51
00:03:07.418 --> 00:03:09.119
He finished sewing the two sides.

52
00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.881
Then he folded the wallet's top flap down.

53
00:03:13.923 --> 00:03:16.285
He marked a spot for the Velcro and stuck it on.

54
00:03:16.305 --> 00:03:20.488
"Done!" Ethan said proudly.

55
00:03:20.508 --> 00:03:23.851
"Can I put my money inside now, Miss Shelly?"

56
00:03:23.871 --> 00:03:26.593
"Sure," Miss Shelly replied.

57
00:03:27.554 --> 00:03:29.556
Izzie and Nina were decorating their wallets.

58
00:03:30.689 --> 00:03:32.690
Izzie cut foam pieces into flowers.

59
00:03:33.511 --> 00:03:34.432
Nina made a cat.

60
00:03:35.552 --> 00:03:37.554
But Ethan wanted to count his money.

61
00:03:38.515 --> 00:03:39.856
He dumped it onto the table.

62
00:03:43.739 --> 00:03:45.540
help you count it," Jason said.

63
00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:48.303
"Put each type of bill in a different stack."

64
00:03:49.203 --> 00:03:51.265
Ethan made a stack of one dollar bills.

65
00:03:52.026 --> 00:03:57.490
"Fifteen!" Next, he made a stack of five dollar bills.

66
00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:03.042
"Four." Finally, he stacked two ten dollar bills.

67
00:04:04.464 --> 00:04:06.685
He counted everything up.

68
00:04:06.705 --> 00:04:08.587
"I have 55 dollars!"

69
00:04:09.588 --> 00:04:13.471
"You need one hundred dollars for the snowboard," Miss Shelly said.

70
00:04:13.491 --> 00:04:16.294
"So how much more money do you need?"

71
00:04:17.615 --> 00:04:19.056
Ethan did the math in his head.

72
00:04:19.076 --> 00:04:21.938
"One hundred minus 55 is 45.

73
00:04:22.058 --> 00:04:29.469
Wow!" He grinned.

74
00:04:29.489 --> 00:04:30.997
"I'm more than halfway there!"
